From 1c7e7c866845a7cebd57bdc65a9b33cd4d66e869 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Veloce PDFium Patches <veloce-pdfium@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 17:23:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Veloce: batch exact strokes across matrix changes

Keep adjacent same-paint stroke commands in one bounded dispatch even when
their object-to-device matrices differ. Carry one exact matrix per command
through CFX_RenderDevice and the AGG driver instead of treating every matrix
change as a batch barrier.

This does not merge path geometry or change painter order. AGG still applies
each command's original matrix and performs a separate rasterization and
source-over composite for every path; the packet only reuses immutable paint
setup and device-owned bounded scratch. Paint, clip, fill, blend,
passthrough, cancellation, and fixed capacity boundaries remain hard flushes.

Add strokeMatrixChangesBatched telemetry so the Q16 dense-tile bottleneck can
be validated before any wider state canonicalization is considered.

